WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.110
- All right, everybody.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.780
Let's close out with a
feel-good story we found online.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:05.448
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.448 --> 00:00:08.760
(upbeat jazzy jingle)

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.400
- A New York man is
combining his love of baking

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.310
with his compassion for kids
to do something very wonderful.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:18.390
He sells these incredible
cookies, which smell so good,

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.090
to send hundreds of sick
children and their families

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.880
on dream vacations to theme
parks all over the country.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.010
Super cool. We have him
on the line right now,

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.600
from Baking Memories 4 Kids,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.800
everybody say hello to Frank,
watching on NBC New York!

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.299
(audience cheers)

00:00:32.299 --> 00:00:33.640
- [Kelly] What's up Frank?

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.410
- Hey Kelly! So good to
be on. Oh, thank you.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:38.970
- Oh my gosh. Well, we love having you,

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.560
and this is such a beautiful
thing you're doing.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.320
So this came from your
own experience, right?

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.500
- Yes. I was out west hiking.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.605
I found a lump in my neck,
Kelly, and I flew home,

00:00:48.605 --> 00:00:52.023
and I went to a bunch of
doctors and I had no idea.

00:00:52.023 --> 00:00:53.550
They finally diagnosed it.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.610
It was advanced stage
three testicular cancer,

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:58.380
and it was going into my brain.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.360
So I did three months of aggressive chemo,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.380
where I couldn't even walk up

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.060
a flight of stairs after a week.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.070
But when I was getting
the chemo, I saw moms

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.410
and the kids also getting
chemo and suffering,

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:10.650
and I knew if I was able
to survive this cancer,

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.320
God gave it to me for a
reason and I would be able

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.540
to help families going
through what I went through,

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.436
and more importantly, the children.

00:01:17.436 --> 00:01:19.405
- Aww.
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:01:19.405 --> 00:01:22.760
- So you're feeling good?
You're feeling good now though?

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.260
- I am so great and I started

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.810
the nonprofit Baking Memories 4 Kids,

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:31.140
and we've been our 11th
season so far, Kelly.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.210
- [Kelly] Wow. (audience
applauds and cheers)

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:37.290
So how exactly does it
work? Tell everybody.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.260
- We bake cookies, and I've had a,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.790
I have a swimming pool company

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.140
that I always used to bake these cookies

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.550
and give them to my customers.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.220
And after I got sick, it
was, instead of making

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.860
a couple thousand cookies,
now we make millions.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.077
To date, we've sold 4.1 million cookies,

00:01:54.077 --> 00:01:57.600
and we make them lovingly
here, Kelly, on the weekends,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.878
and we sell them online
and all of that money

00:01:59.878 --> 00:02:04.140
goes towards funding, it's
a week-long, amazing trip

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.870
for the entire family, all expenses paid,

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.450
Universal Studios, every amusement park,

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.700
and Baking Memories pays
for the entire trip.

00:02:13.036 --> 00:02:15.010
- [Kelly] That's incredible,
Frank, thank you so much.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.583
Wait, I'm gonna taste
one because, well, I can.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.130
Oh my God, I love that it's
crunchy. This is really good.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.430
And I don't usually eat
cookies, so thank you.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:30.150
Thank you, Frank. You have
such a beautiful heart.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.340
Congrats on beating cancer as well, man.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.540
That's, what a beautiful thing

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.100
that you went through something so tragic,

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.050
but you turned it around to
make it something beautiful

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.430
for others and yourself.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.383
Wow. I'm loving your post right now.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.710
Well, that's not all Frank.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.600
Our season-long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.100
makers of Precise, the go-to pen

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.570
of the Kelly Clarkson Show want to honor

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.850
truly unstoppable people
just like yourself.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.490
So they're gonna be writing
Baking Memories for Kids

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.140
a check for a thousand dollars.
(audience cheers and claps)

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.997
- Awesome. Thank you so much.

00:02:59.202 --> 00:03:00.726
- [Kelly] Thank you so much, Frank.

00:03:00.726 --> 00:03:02.417
Have a blessed holiday season.

00:03:02.417 --> 00:03:04.145
Thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:04.145 --> 00:03:07.193
Taraji P. Henson, Matt
Iceman, Killer Mike,

00:03:07.193 --> 00:03:10.267
Laura Terry and the
Tanners, and our day of elf.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:13.122
Y'all have a great day and if
it's not, try and change it.

